{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And he said to his people.</b> The Egyptians." "<b>Behold, the people.</b> The word עם is not in construct state; rather, בני ישראל is its explanation and an added clarification, like \"אהיה אשר אהיה\" (below 3:14), \"אשר התהלכו אבותי לפניו אברהם ויצחק\" (Genesis 48:15)." "<b>Than we.</b> Every ממנו in the books of the people of the East: if it is a sign of plural, the nun is weak, as is the rule, to distinguish between it and between ממנו פנה (Zechariah 10:4), which is a sign of singular that does not occur before the attached pronoun, which has a dagesh as is the rule. And in all the books of the West both are with dagesh, whether it is a sign of singular or a sign of plural. And it should be so, for ממנו in the singular has a dagesh contrary to the rule, for the word אני is weak, and likewise the word \"נחני ד׳\" (Genesis 24:27). Now, the word מן is doubled; the nun is given a dagesh in מִמֶּנִּי for the lack of the other nun, as if it were מִמֶּנְנִי, for the first nun comes with the letter mem as if it is מן, [and] ני as the sign of the speaker. If so, \"איש ממנו\" (Genesis 23:6), which is plural, is as if it is מִמֶּנְנוּ. And the reason the nun of מִמֶּנּוּ has a dagesh is the assimilation of the heh in absence, for he says מִן יִשְׁמְרוּ, \"אֲשֶׁר יִקְרְאוֹ\" (Jeremiah 23:6), \"אַיּוֹב יִרְדְּפוֹ\" (Hosea 8:3). And this is the minority, for the majority: \"יִשְׁמְרֵהוּ\" (Psalms 41:3); rather, יִשְׁמְרוּ is a shortened form, like \"וְהִנֵּהוּ עֹשֶׂה מְלָאכָה\" (Jeremiah 10:3), which is like וְהִנֵּה הוּא, \"וְהִנֵּה נִצָּב\" (Numbers 22:6). And sometimes they add a nun: \"יִשְׁחֲרוּנְנִי וְלֹא יִמְצָאוּנְנִי\" (Proverbs 1:28), \"תְּכַרְכְנִי נַפְשְׁךָ\" (Genesis 27:19), like תְּבָרְכְנִי, \"זֹבֵחַ תּוֹדָה יְכַבְּדֵנְנִי\" (Psalms 50:23), יְסוֹבְבֶנְהוּ, יְבֹנְנֵהוּ, יִצְּרֶנְהוּ (Deuteronomy 32:10). And sometimes they assimilate the heh into the nun: \"וְלֹא יִשְׁמְרֶנּוּ בַּעְלָיו\" (below 21:29)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "The text contains a fragmented clause 'להפריש בינו, ובין' with a gap; translated hyper-literally as printed. The parsing of the dagesh/weak nun argument follows the manuscripts as given; several internal clauses are elliptical and have been rendered verbatim without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:56.858543424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}